{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q418094","formula":"ZnFe₂O₄","hill":"Fe2O4Zn","elements":["O","Fe","Zn"],"composition":{"O":4.0,"Fe":2.0,"Zn":1.0},"names":{"en":"Franklinite","ru":"Франклинит","uk":"Франклініт"},"descriptions":{"en":"Franklinite is an oxide mineral belonging to the normal spinel subgroup's iron (Fe) series, with the formula ZnFe3+2O4. As with another spinel member magnetite, both ferrous (2+) and ferric (3+) iron may be present in Franklinite samples. Divalent iron and/or manganese (Mn) may commonly accompany zinc (Zn) and trivalent manganese may substitute for some ferric iron.","ru":"Франклини́т(ZnFe2O4) — минерал класса окислов. Был впервые найден в 1819 году в шахтах Стерлинг-Хилл и Франклин в штате Нью-Джерси, США, отсюда и название.","uk":"Франклініт (англ. franklinite) — мінерал, оксид цинку та заліза координаційної будови із ряду магнетиту, групи шпінелі (феришпінелі). Цинкова руда."},"fame":21,"pubchemCid":null,"mass":null,"charge":0,"smiles":null,"inchikey":null,"iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q12089225","names":{"en":"mineral species","ru":"действительный вид минералов","uk":"мінеральний вид"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"crystal","source":"materialsproject","ref":"mp-19313","atoms":65,"license":"CC BY 4.0, Materials Project"},"structure":{"cell":[[8.436,0.0,0.0],[0.0,8.436,0.0],[0.0,0.0,8.436]],"kind":"crystal","atoms":[{"x":6.327,"y":6.327,"z":6.327,"el":"Zn"},{"x":0.0,"y":4.218,"z":0.0,"el":"Zn"},{"x":0.0,"y":4.218,"z":8.436,"el":"Zn"},{"x":8.436,"y":4.218,"z":0.0,"el":"Zn"},{"x":8.436,"y":4.218,"z":8.436,"el":"Zn"},{"x":7.381,"y":7.381,"z":1.054,"el":"Fe"},{"x":7.381,"y":5.272,"z":3.163,"el":"Fe"},{"x":1.054,"y":5.272,"z":5.272,"el":"Fe"},{"x":1.054,"y":3.163,"z":3.163,"el":"Fe"},{"x":5.354,"y":7.3,"z":1.136,"el":"O"},{"x":7.3,"y":7.3,"z":3.082,"el":"O"},{"x":7.3,"y":5.354,"z":1.136,"el":"O"},{"x":0.973,"y":5.191,"z":3.245,"el":"O"},{"x":7.463,"y":5.191,"z":5.191,"el":"O"},{"x":7.463,"y":3.245,"z":3.245,"el":"O"},{"x":5.354,"y":5.354,